/* The Entertainment room's list — what Ric has watched and what is queued up.

   This file is the committed truth. The page renders it, and an edit made on the
   page (adding a title, moving one from the queue to watched) is layered on top of
   it at read time rather than rewritten into it — same shape as the climbing
   section, where the committed history stands on its own and the service only ever
   adds to it. Two things can supply that layer:

     · the Worker's /movies endpoint, when it is deployed — public to read,
       Ric's token to write, so an edit follows him between phone and laptop and
       visitors see it too;
     · this browser's localStorage, when the Worker is not reachable — which is
       every edit made before the Worker ships, and any made while it is down.

   Either way the edits stay OUT of this file until someone commits them. The page's
   owner panel has an Export button that prints a replacement for this file with the
   pending edits folded in; paste it over this one and the layer empties itself.

   Fields:
     id      slug, and the key both storage layers use — do not renumber or reuse
     title   as it should read on the page
     status  "watched" | "watchlist"
     count   how many of a franchise Ric counted ("Saw(1-10)" → 10)
     series  true where he wrote "(all)" and a number would be a guess
     where   how he'd get at it: a service name, or "Buy"
     pick    he starred it — top of the queue
     note    anything the raw list said that the fields above cannot hold

   Titles are his list, lightly corrected for spelling and casing. Where a title was
   ambiguous it was left as typed rather than guessed at — see README. */
